  "transcript": "Sometimes, it's less work to just do the task. I can use AI to build something that does it for me, but if it breaks, or the way I want to do the job changes, I am still the one who's got to go back and fix it. Say I automate how I organize files for a project. If I'm still moving folders around and changing what goes where, I've now got to update the automation as well. For something I do all the time, that might be worth it. But if it's an occasional job, And I'm still figuring out how I want it done. I might be better off leaving it manual for now You guys tell me what's something you've deliberately kept doing yourself because the automation wasn't worth looking after",
